A||||3||slick||84 SE - distributor rotor swapped ?
Z||000000||slick||08-01-99||03:09 PM||||i just bought a 84 se. it doesn't run, the previous owner said she was driving down the road, saw a puff of smoke in back, and it just quit running. i have been piddling around with it and found a lot of spliced wiring and no longer used terminals. after some work it will now crank but not fire. the spark looks a little weak but i havn't tested it yet. i went to get a new rotor, and come to find out that the rotor and distributor are out of an 82-83 2.5l firebird or 6000. is it possible that my engine could also have been swapped from an 82 or 83 ? Also, this engine has an "edelbrock performance pontiac tbi " intake. has anybody come across one of these before? thanks
Z||000001||fred||08-01-99||09:02 PM||||the distributer itself or ignition coil have some probs.Also the timing good be out.Check ,reset computer ...(disconnect voltage for 3-5 mins)could be fuel pump. the wiring sounds like it could give you a real headache if spliced ,etc .If you want get a wire harness from a boneyard for your se .the engine itself may not have the sensors an original 84 se would have. Iwould start all over with the wiring .get a Haynes manual see if you engine has all sensors (The manual will help)    good luck<br>I used to have a 84 se similar probs occured i just replaced engine sold it and got myself 86 se 2.8 replaced that engine with 3.1          remember this fiero are high maintenance vehicles.   only my opinion<p>FRED
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||08-01-99||10:22 PM||||Is there an echo?
Z||000003||Dale||08-02-99||12:59 AM||||If it used to run it will run again with that motor.  First question is were did the puff of smoke come from.  there are three basic functions that keep almost any engine running.  Electrical, fuel, and mechanical.  Sounds to me like something electrical.  You might get out the ohm meter and start checking wires.  Have fun!!
